From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:56:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Drop stylesheet loads for removed link nodes

load_resource handed a Resource::Css to add_stylesheet_for_node
without checking that the <link> still exists. Script can remove the
link while its sheet is still in flight. When the node was dropped,
its slotmap key went stale and add_stylesheet_for_node panicked with
"invalid SlotMap key used". When the node was only detached, its sheet
styled a document the link was no longer part of. Nothing removes that
sheet, because the removal ran before the sheet was registered.

The load is now dropped unless the node is a live element in the
document, as Chrome does. Inserting the link again starts a new fetch
through process_added_subtree. A Resource::Css with no node id is
dropped instead of unwrapped.
---
 src/document.rs | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/document.rs b/src/document.rs
index 9f10ab5..32e4c53 100644
--- a/src/document.rs
+++ b/src/document.rs
@@ -2101,7 +2101,22 @@ impl BaseDocument {

         match resource {
             Resource::Css(css) => {
-                let node_id = res.node_id.unwrap();
+                // Script can remove the <link> while its sheet is
+                // still in flight. A dropped node leaves a stale key, and
+                // indexing it panicked in the middle of handle_messages; a
+                // detached one would apply its sheet to a document it is no
+                // longer part of. Chrome drops that load too. Inserting the
+                // link again starts a new fetch (process_added_subtree).
+                let Some(node_id) = res.node_id else {
+                    return;
+                };
+                let connected = self
+                    .nodes
+                    .get(node_id)
+                    .is_some_and(|node| node.is_element() && node.flags.is_in_document());
+                if !connected {
+                    return;
+                }
                 self.add_stylesheet_for_node(css, node_id);
             }
             Resource::ImportedCss(import_rule, sheet) => {
